JOB 30 – SHIP & SHOWCASE (FINAL)

1. Introduction
Job 30 is the final project demonstration of the Python programming course.
In this job, students present the working project developed during the project sprint.
The main purpose is to demonstrate that the program solves a real-life problem and works correctly.
2. Learning Objectives
Demonstrate the completed Python project.
Explain the problem and its solution.
Show the working of the program.
Test the program using real input.
Handle incorrect or invalid input.
Explain the important features of the project.
3. Operation Sequence – Demo Day
The final demonstration is divided into four operations.
Operation
Activity
OP 10
Handover checks – Test another team's project on your computer.
OP 20
Showcase – Present your project for five minutes.
OP 30
Teaching round – Explain one important thing learned during the course.
OP 40
Dispatch – Discuss what happens to the project after the demonstration.
4. The Five-Minute Project Demonstration
The project presentation should follow five steps.
Step 1: The Person
Explain the real-life problem.
Mention:
Who faces the problem?
What is the problem?
What happens because of it?
Step 2: Run It
Demonstrate the working program.
Give real input.
Run the program.
Show the output.
Step 3: Break It
Give incorrect input intentionally and show how the program handles the error.
The program should display a clear error message instead of crashing.
Step 4: One Line You're Proud Of
Explain one important function or class developed in the project.
Also explain why that particular feature was developed.
Step 5: What You Cut
Explain which features were not included in the final project and why.
This shows the importance of project planning and time management.
Conclusion
Job 30 is the final stage of the Python programming course.
It provides an opportunity to demonstrate practical programming skills through a working project. It also develops communication, problem-solving and presentation skills.
